      "content": "It can take several hours to propagate DNS changes to cover the entire internet. This delay is due to the way DNS is cached and propagated across different networks and devices. When you update an A record, the change is sent to a central registry like-root servers, which then propagate the update to other servers, and eventually, to users' devices. To speed up the process, you can consider contacting your Internet Service Provider (ISP) or registering for a Cloudflare or other DNS service that offers caching and propagation optimization.",
