      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The inconsistencies in propagation times can be due to the variability in timestamp differences between different regions, cache sizes, and network latencies. However, the most significant contributor to delays is often the \" wink-of-the-eye\" problem, where it takes some time (usually a few hours) for caches to realize that the data they're serving is outdated and needs to be updated. This can cause widespread inconsistencies, as not all caches respond to the update at the same time.",
      "source": "target",
